Batch instanced image meshes and give split atomic-mode instances tight bounds.

- include/rive/renderer.hpp: ImageMeshInstances mesh bounds: optional local-space bounds of the mesh the instances draw, so renderers that split instances can give each one tight pixel bounds
- include/rive/renderer.hpp: ImageMeshInstances mesh bounds: storage for the optional mesh bounds
- source/renderer/rive_renderer.cpp: Atomic mode instanced image meshes: give each split instance tight pixel bounds from the mesh bounds instead of fullscreen, so non-overlapping instances share a draw group and skip the per-instance atomic barriers (render pass restarts on WebGPU)
- source/renderer/render_context.cpp: Image mesh batching: image meshes are batchable like other single ElementRange draw types (image rects still aren't)
- source/renderer/render_context.cpp: Image mesh batching: adjacent image mesh draws merge only with the same vertex, uv and index buffers, index count, blend mode and draw contents
- source/renderer/render_context.cpp: Image mesh batching: splice adjacent compatible image mesh draws into one instanced draw

